          "summary": "Keep the books for your business",
          "details_markdown": "Budgets set up as a sole trader or limited company can now turn on double-entry books. Open More, tap \"Enable double-entry books\" — OpenBudget sets up your chart of accounts once (this can't be undone) — and your Books are ready. Record money in and money out as journals that always balance, see everything you owe and own grouped in your chart of accounts, and check the trial balance for any date you like; OpenBudget tells you at a glance whether your books balance. Posted entries are locked for your records, so mistakes are corrected with a reversal instead of an edit, and you can set a lock date to freeze the periods you've already closed.\n\nJournals now show their lines, so you can see exactly what went in and out of each account. Drafts can be reopened and finished later: OpenBudget fills the entry back in and saves over the same draft instead of making a second one. Your books' lock date is remembered, and the Books screen shows it at a glance.",
